# === 2K GAMES (NBA 2K, WWE 2K, etc.) ===
# !! DO NOT ADD base domains - breaks matchmaking and CDN !!
# 2K Games uses Akamai/AWS CDNs that MUST resolve to geo-local IPs.
# Routing through VPS causes: matchmaking failures, "unable to connect to server"
#
# Excluded domains (must resolve normally via real DNS):
#   - 2k.com, www.2k.com              (website / account)
#   - 2ksports.com                     (game services)
#   - take2games.com                   (parent company, CDN routing)
#   - a978.i6g1.akamai.net            (Akamai CDN for game assets)
#   - Any *.2k.com subdomains         (matchmaking, leaderboards, etc.)
#
# If you MUST unblock 2K account pages only (NOT game traffic), you can
# ONLY add the single website domain. But this is NOT recommended:
#   __VPS_IP__ www.2k.com
#
# Why it breaks:
#   - NBA 2K matchmaking uses region-based server selection
#   - CDN assets (rosters, updates) come from geo-located Akamai nodes
#   - Routing via VPS makes the game think you're in the wrong region
#   - Results in: "Unable to connect to 2K servers", timeout errors

